                g35: 'Check yourself. Name the four factors that spread belief traditions around the world: migration, forced migration, proselytism and colonialism. What did the Indian Act do to Indigenous ceremonies, and when? It banned the potlatch and other ceremonies from 1885 to 1951. Exit ticket: pick one tradition in your community, like a church, mosque, temple or gurdwara near you. Which of the four factors most likely brought it here?',
                g68: 'Answer in your notes, then compare with a partner.\n\n- Name the **four factors** that gave belief traditions global reach, with one example each.\n- What did the Indian Act do to Indigenous ceremonies, and in which years?\n- Explain how Mother Teresa\'s belief led to a specific action.\n\n**Exit ticket:** pick one tradition in your community. Which factor most likely brought it here? If people changed traditions along the way, that is **conversion** — changing from one belief tradition, or none, to another.\n\n**Think:** can the same tradition arrive in a country by more than one of the four factors? Give an example.'
