                2: '"A rule that treats everyone the same is not always fair." Using the Multani case, Bill 21, and the idea of sincerity of belief, evaluate this statement. Consider the strongest argument for equal treatment (same rule for all) and the strongest argument for accommodation (adjusting the rule), and defend your own view on how Canadian schools should handle religious practice.',
                3: '"A rule that treats everyone the same is not always fair." Using **all three** of the Multani case, Bill 21, and the idea of sincerity of belief, evaluate this statement. Consider the strongest argument for equal treatment (same rule for all) and the strongest argument for accommodation (adjusting the rule), and defend your own view on how Canadian schools should handle religious practice. Use at least **two** lesson terms correctly and give **one** example of a condition that keeps an accommodation safe.',
