                2: 'Identifies the tradition and meaning of all four items (mantras: Hindu/Buddhist sacred sounds; bindi and henna: Hindu and South Asian religious and ceremonial markers; rosary: Catholic prayer beads; blanket pattern: specific First Nations designs with family, clan or spiritual meaning) · explains effects using appropriation and commercialization (meaning stripped, outsiders profit, no credit or benefit) · judges "celebrating" unfair without consultation, context or benefit · gives three specific changes.',
                3: '…plus a third lesson term, a comparison with a real case (kuffiyeh or Nike), and each change tied to the problem it fixes.',
                4: '…plus a defended ranking of the four products using the lesson\'s principle, a test of the principle against the Nike case, and a real local example.'
