                2: 'Identifies the calendar error (Diwali is a lunisolar autumn festival), the significance error (different festivals flattened into \'light\'), and the practice error (Holi colour is the observance itself, not decoration), plus the Holy Week and Purim timing · proposes two spring festivals on or near their dates (e.g. Holi Mar 22, Nowruz Mar 21, Purim Mar 23) each with its significance and a real practice · answers the \'just fun\' defence: fun is fine when the community leads and the meaning travels with the practice; copying colour and lamps without their stories turns practice into decoration.',
                3: '…plus two vocabulary terms used correctly and at least two accurate dates.',
                4: '…plus a reasoned set of conditions for combining festivals (community leadership, explanation of meaning, keeping distinct festivals distinct) and an honest test of those conditions against a real local event.'
