                2: 'Salah: set sun-based times, wudu (water), a clean space, facing Mecca, about 5–10 minutes each · tefillin and the Shema: weekday morning, private space, a few minutes, the tefillin themselves · Five Ks: no break, worn continuously, relevant to dress and safety policies · sunrise ceremony: outdoors, facing east, before dawn or at sunrise, tobacco or smudge · a rewritten policy covering timing (breaks at the times the practice requires, not only scheduled ones), space (a clean quiet room with a sink; outdoor space before or after shift), articles of faith (dress and safety policies accommodate them), and accommodation language (up to undue hardship) · explains that performed observances need time and space while worn ones need policies allowing the articles at all times (uniforms, helmets, security, grooming) and raise visibility and prejudice questions, so accommodation looks different for each.',
