                2: 'Five differences each tied to the Council: liturgy reforms (English, priest facing the people); the theology of the laity for lay readers and ministers; the decline in vowed religious and rise of lay vocations for lay teachers; lay participation in governance for the parish council; Nostra Aetate (1965) for the interfaith food drive · a fair \'what we lost\' panel (Latin Mass, chant, the sisters\' service) presented with respect beside the Council\'s reasons · a comparison showing both movements changed language, roles, and openness to other faiths, while Catholicism kept the priesthood and sacraments and Reform changed law and ordination more radically.',
                3: 'Everything in Level 2 · plus at least two lesson terms used correctly.',
                4: 'Everything in Level 3 · plus a reasoned separation of Council causes from social causes (smaller families, more options for women, secularization) with evidence · a real example of change in a place you know.'
