                g35: 'Sacred places are not only buildings. In the Haudenosaunee creation story, the land grows on a turtle\'s back, so North America itself, Turtle Island, is sacred and alive. The Western Wall in Jerusalem is the last wall of the ancient Temple; Jews pray facing it and tuck written prayers into its cracks, and every synagogue\'s Ark faces Jerusalem. Hindus see the Ganges River as a goddess, and bathing in it is believed to make a person pure. Think: why does the Ark face Jerusalem?',
