                4: 'Reflect on the course (A4.4). Using at least two of the four unit assignments and one of this lesson\'s cases, evaluate your own research, inquiry, and communication skills: which step of the research process you did best, which source question changed how you read, what you would do differently, and what question about belief traditions remains for you. Then connect your remaining question to the idea of sacred place — what would you need to see, visit, or ask to answer it?\n\nWrite one to two paragraphs. Then turn the lesson\'s method on yourself: this unit taught you to describe a place first and then explain it by belief, and to read who was listened to (the Somme) and who was not (Ipperwash). Evaluate whether your own research listened to community voices or relied on outside accounts, and design the first step of a research plan that would answer your remaining question — the place you would go, the person you would ask, and the question you would bring.'
